 {"id": "RATE-LIMIT-001", "title": "P1 \u2014 Default HTTP rate limit is 100 req/min and 429s are NEVER logged: a bulk ingest loses ~78% of writes while the daemon log shows nothing wrong. cli/http.ts:391 `requestsPerMinute: options.rateLimit ?? 100`.", "priority": "P1", "status": "complete", "created_at": "2026-09-27T16:14:38.590891+00:00", "created_by": null, "complexity": 2, "detail": {"fingerprint": "03074e21c5d3143ae70175c9818ea6a6779672c319a97d68c37f7868e634ad50"}, "reasoning": "Third-party review (carterlasalle method), clean clone of main @ 42cea0a, scratch daemons :3997 (default) and :3996 (--rate-limit 6000). MEASURED at the default: 500 sequential authenticated writes -> accepted=111, refused=389 all HTTP 429 with `Retry-After: 1`; only 29 of the 100 intended distinct keys ever landed. Response headers confirm the bucket: `X-RateLimit-Limit: 100`, `X-RateLimit-Remaining: 0`. MEASURED at --rate-limit 6000 on the SAME build: 300 sequential -> 300/300 in 2.83s (106 writes/s); 200 concurrent with 32 workers -> 200/200 in 0.67s (299 writes/s); write latency mean 9.9ms / median 9.4ms / p95 13.0ms / max 15.7ms; 651 rows on disk, 0 unparseable. So the ENGINE is not the constraint at this scale \u2014 the default limiter is, and raising it is a config change, not a code change. TWO DEFECTS, one row: (a) 100 req/min per bucket is the wrong shape for the stated multi-agent use case, and because the localhost/tailnet side door arrives as 127.0.0.1 the whole co-located fleet shares ONE bucket rather than getting one each; (b) 429 refusals appear nowhere in the daemon log, so an operator watching logs sees a healthy server while writes silently vanish from the caller's perspective. Log limit/remaining/retry-after at WARN regardless of what the limit becomes (~1h). No existing board row covers either half (grep for ratelimit/429 found only incidental matches: a CI flake title, PUSH-001's per-namespace autopush interval, and DB-SUPA-3's route listing). EVIDENCE LEVEL: measured live; footer commit 42cea0a, Node v22.22.3, pnpm 12.4.2, 2026-09-27, ports 3996/3997.", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T16:14:38.590891+00:00", "worker_status": "complete", "completed_at": "2026-09-27T22:15:01Z", "commit_hash": "85ab900", "files_changed": ["src/auth/ratelimit.ts", "src/auth/ratelimit.test.ts"], "lines_added": 134, "lines_removed": 0, "guard_result": "PASS \u2014 GitReins verdict b1753722: tier1 secrets + tests (179 suites/1430 tests); tier2 PASS", "ci_result": "RED \u2014 run 36354878908 exact HEAD d16a531 failed only AGENTS.md count assertion (live 179 suites/1430 tests); count follow-up filed", "worker_summary": "Worker rework committed 85ab900: every 429 emits JSON console.warn with event, IP, limit, remaining=0, retryAfter; 3 regression tests; focused 9/9, tsc clean, prettier clean.", "foreman_note": "Implementation commit 85ab900 + GitReins evidence commit d16a531 pushed; verdict b1753722 passed. CI count drift is a separate follow-up: /tmp/rate-limit-001-agents-edit.md records the sanctioned AGENTS.md correction and exact red step. Default 100 req/min was not changed; this tick landed the silent-429 observability half.", "attempts": 2, "dispatched_at": "2026-09-27T21:43:55Z"}
 {"id": "README-A2A-001", "title": "P3 \u2014 README \"Multi-Agent Ready\" reads as agent-to-agent protocol, but a tree-wide grep on main finds A2A 0 / ACP 0 / AgentCard 0 / dead-letter 0 / DLQ 0 files. One clause would scope the claim to what ships.", "priority": "P3", "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-27T16:14:38.590891+00:00", "created_by": null, "complexity": 1, "detail": {"fingerprint": "694e34a3cbc940f2af9f0b369102ffd92f53862815948a8c4c11dd49b24a5928"}, "reasoning": "Third-party review (carterlasalle method), clean clone of main @ 42cea0a. README Features list claims 'Multi-Agent Ready \u2014 HTTP mode with worktrees for concurrent access'. A reader takes that as agents negotiating with each other (A2A/AgentCard discovery); the actual meaning is a SHARED STORE with per-namespace isolation and no wire protocol for agent-to-agent messaging. ABSENCE VERIFIED BY GREP (absence is only evidence after a grep): A2A 0 files, ACP 0 files, AgentCard 0 files, dead-letter 0 files, DLQ 0 files; idempotency present in 9 files and event-stream in 5, so the grep is discriminating rather than blanket-negative. FIX: state the scope in one clause, e.g. 'shared store with per-namespace isolation; no agent-to-agent protocol'. ~10 min. EVIDENCE LEVEL: measured (grep over src/ at 42cea0a); no live exercise needed.", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T16:14:38.590891+00:00"}
 {"id": "SUPA6-DECLARE-GAP-001", "title": "P2 \u2014 DB-SUPA-6 (declared DDL surface) is marked complete, but on a fresh install there is NO discoverable way to declare a table: the per-namespace OpenAPI spec returns paths: 0 and no CLI or HTTP declare verb was found.", "priority": "P2", "status": "pending", "created_at": "2026-09-27T16:14:38.590891+00:00", "created_by": null, "complexity": 3, "detail": {"fingerprint": "08cad1141de2d694e16083779b581c9dcfb286356a75954e7824a6151c1f31d5"}, "reasoning": "Third-party review (carterlasalle method), clean clone of main @ 42cea0a, authed scratch daemon :3995. OBSERVED: GET /api/ns/review/openapi.json -> 200, valid OpenAPI doc, `paths: 0`, with info.description stating it is 'Generated from the declared table registry (namespaces/<ns>/tables/*.table.json). PostgREST-style filters/order/paging on every table.' A fresh namespace dir contains only .git, _audit/, manifest.json, raw_note/ \u2014 no tables/ dir, so the empty spec is internally consistent. The gap is discoverability: `duckbrain help` exposes remember/recall/namespace/squash/query and NO tables verb (grep for declare|create|add under src/cli/ found nothing); POST /api/ns/review/tables -> 404 because the mount is relative (POST /:table inserts a ROW into an existing table, it does not declare one). So the declared-table REST layer is unreachable from a fresh install by any documented path, even though SUPA-6, DOC-5 and DB-SUPA-3 all read complete. MY WRONG GUESS, RECORDED: I assumed POST /api/ns/<ns>/tables declared a table; it does not. FIX DIRECTION: ship one example .table.json in the scaffold and/or a `duckbrain tables declare` verb so the spec is self-teaching (0.5-1d). VERIFY: a declaration path may exist somewhere I did not search \u2014 confirm before dispatching. EVIDENCE LEVEL: measured live (:3995) + grep over src/ at 42cea0a.", "updated_at": "2026-09-27T16:14:38.590891+00:00"}
